From: Cidwel <cidwel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi: let the USB-C connector sink power

Source-only, the phone powers a laptop over USB-C instead of charging from
it, and drains its battery to UVLO overnight. Dual role with try-sink, the
same ports as the sm8250 Xiaomi trees upstream. Verified on the surya by
patching the installed DTB first: charger online, +985 mA, role swappable
both ways from sysfs.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi	2026-09-05 11:55:25.151107734 +0200
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi	2026-09-05 11:55:25.159445773 +0200
@@ -601,12 +601,25 @@
 	connector {
 		compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 
-		power-role = "source";
+		/*
+		 * Dual, and asking for power first. As a source-only port this
+		 * phone won a PD negotiation against a laptop's USB-C port and
+		 * spent a night powering the laptop until the cell hit UVLO
+		 * (measured 2026-09-05: charger online=0, current_now -366 mA,
+		 * laptop side "ucsi-source-psy: Charging"). With this, the same
+		 * cable charges it at ~1 A, and the role can still be swapped
+		 * from /sys/class/typec/port0/power_role.
+		 */
+		power-role = "dual";
+		try-power-role = "sink";
 		data-role = "dual";
 		self-powered;
 
 		source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 			       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
+		sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
+			     PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
+		op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
 
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
